# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DUET — repository hygiene
#
# The working tree carries ~3.4 GB of data and intermediate results. None of it
# belongs on GitHub: the inputs are public and re-downloadable (see README), and
# every table here is reproducible from the scripts. What IS tracked from
# results/ is the small stuff a reader wants without re-running anything:
# the summaries, the concordance tables, the null/simulation scores, and figures.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- never, under any circumstances ---
*codex*
*Codex*
*CODEX*

# --- data (public, re-downloadable; see README for provenance) ---
data/
*.h5ad
*.mtx
*.mtx.gz
*.rds
*.tar
*.loom

# --- benchmark working directories (regenerate with bench_mast_*.py / .R) ---
bench/
**/_mast_work/
_tmp_*/

# --- backups made during the July 2026 refactor ---
code_backup_*/
results_backup_*/

# --- exploratory subproject, superseded by the three-dataset comparison ---
SmallComapre/

# --- python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- R ---
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/

# --- results: NOT tracked ---
# Code only for now. Everything under results*/ is derived from data that is
# either unpublished (the pancreas/PDAC object) or re-downloadable (Kang,
# Crowell, the muscat simulation), and every table is reproducible from the
# scripts. Revisit when the preprint goes up.
results/
results_kang/
results_crowell/
results_sim/
results_null/
de_*_all_celltypes.csv
comparison_per_gene.csv
consensus_genes.csv
mast_all_celltypes*.csv
*.log

# --- the DE_Compare project's own documentation (Hungarian) ---
# The benchmark write-up with all the validation findings. Belongs to the
# analysis project, not to the DUET library; README.md in the repo is the
# library's own English documentation.
BENCHMARK.hu.md

# --- legacy back-compat shim, removed from the repo by the author ---
# Kept on disk so the old `from CustomDE.scpyde import run_scpyde` path keeps
# working locally (e.g. for scPipeline.py); not shipped in the library.
CustomDE/

# --- Phase 2.5 evidence pack (derived; regenerate with collect_evidence.py) ---
evidence/
collect_evidence.py

# --- benchmark / analysis harness: NOT part of the DUET tool ---
# These live in this working folder and produce the validation evidence, but the
# repo is the DUET library only. Kept on disk, untracked.
add_mast_and_rebuild.py
bench_mast_export.py
bench_mast_report.py
bench_mast_run.R
build_crowell_h5ad.py
build_kang_h5ad.py
build_sim_h5ad.py
evaluate_sim.py
get_crowell.R
make_heatmaps.py
make_volcano.py
null_calibration.py
rebuild_comparison.py
rerun_scpyde_rebuild.py
run_de_comparison.py
run_mast_dataset.py
simulate_muscat.R

# --- os / editor noise ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Ductal permutation-null diagnostic (analysis project, not the library)
diag_ductal.py

# Manuscript draft (analysis project, not the library)
MANUSCRIPT.md

# Manuscript build artefacts (analysis project, not the library)
DUET_manuscript.docx
build_manuscript_docx.js
build_docx_data.py
make_fig1.py
make_fig2.py
_render/
